		{
			"to": "blood/recombinant-factor",
			"why": "The clotting factor missing in hemophilia A was made from a cloned human gene, the method of this frame applied to a protein too large and too scarce to get any other way."
		},
		{
			"to": "food/gm-crops",
			"why": "Engineered crops are made by borrowing another plasmid, the tumor-inducing ring of Agrobacterium, to carry a chosen gene into a plant as pSC101 carried one into a bacterium."
		},
		{
			"to": "chemistry/pcr",
			"why": "Cloning in bacteria was the only way to get many copies of one stretch of DNA until PCR copied it in a tube; Mullis's first working run in 1983 was on a piece of a plasmid."
		},
		{
			"to": "biology/asilomar",
			"why": "Cohen and Boyer, who first cloned recombinant DNA in 1973, signed the committee letter of July 1974 asking scientists to defer such work, which called for the meeting held at Asilomar in 1975."
		}
